      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14155061/assets/93a73e4b7458251fdb96891e2b00af4fd5ecf6a442aed9fb7c289ca25ae0e389.png)\n\nUse the model above to find the value of $\\dfrac{11}{14} \\div \\dfrac{3}{7}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The denominators are $7$ and $14.$ We can make a common denominator of $14.$\n\nWe split the shape on the right of the division sign into $2$ parts horizontally:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14155061/assets/a9867f3e62605ccbaad6fdc6a1925173a460f287e36b8cc563ab62bb3074a13c.png)\n\nSo, our division problem now is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\color{red}11}{14} \\div \\dfrac{\\color{blue}6}{14}.\n$$\n\nSince the denominators are equal, this is equivalent to\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}11} \\div {\\color{blue}6} = 1\\,\\dfrac56.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{11}{14} \\div \\dfrac{3}{7} = 1\\,\\dfrac56 \\, .\n$$",
